   photoshop:Instructions="To ensure consistent colour, both on screen and in reproduction, the photographic images supplied on this disc have been prepared within a closed loop colour-managed workflow.  All images are embedded with an Adobe (1998) RGB colour profile. This is a wide gamut colour space which shows the maximum range of viewable colours.   Unsharp masking (USM) is an essential part of the reproduction process and should be applied after resizing for actual output. These images have not been sharpened.   When handling these images please observe the following: â€¢ Always view images on a recently calibrated monitor.  â€¢ When opening images in Photoshop, or similar image editing program, the embedded profile should be converted to your working colour space.   â€¢ Unsharp masking (USM) should be applied after resizing. â€¢ RGB files require professional conversion to a CMYK profile before printing."
